	"packageName": "eslint-plugin-hyper-fetch",
	"readme": [
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "# 🧹 Hyper Fetch ESLint Plugin\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>ESLint rules to enforce HyperFetch best practices and catch type issues early.</b>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch?style=flat\" alt=\"GitHub stars\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/eslint-plugin-hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/eslint-plugin-hyper-fetch\" alt=\"npm version\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch/blob/main/License.md\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/license/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\" alt=\"License\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch\">\n    <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/typescript-%23007ACC.svg?logo=typescript&logoColor=white\" alt=\"TypeScript\" />\n  </a>\n</p>\n\n## 📖 About\n\nThis ESLint plugin provides static analysis rules specific to HyperFetch. It catches generic type issues like typos,\nmissing values, or incorrect usage of "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createClient`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createRequest`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " type parameters before they cause runtime\nerrors.\n\n## 🎯 Key Capabilities\n\n- 🔮 **Catch type bugs before they run** — Validates "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createClient`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " and "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`createRequest`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " generic parameters at lint time\n- ✨ **No more typo-induced "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`any`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "** — Detects misspelled keys like "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`rsponse`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": " instead of "
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "`response`"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n- 🔧 **Plug and play** — Use the recommended preset or configure rules one by one\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```bash\nnpm install -D eslint-plugin-hyper-fetch\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```json\n{\n  \"extends\": [\"plugin:hyper-fetch/recommended\"]\n}\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\nOr configure individual rules:\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```json\n{\n  \"plugins\": [\"hyper-fetch\"],\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"hyper-fetch/client-generic-types\": \"error\",\n    \"hyper-fetch/request-generic-types\": \"error\"\n  }\n}\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## 📚 Documentation\n\n- [ESLint Plugin Docs](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/integrations/plugin-eslint)\n- [Getting Started](https://hyperfetch.bettertyped.com/docs/getting-started/quick-start)\n\n## 💡 Examples\n\n### Catches incorrect generic types\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\n// ❌ This will be flagged by hyper-fetch/request-generic-types\nconst getUser = client.createRequest<{\n  rsponse: User; // Typo: \"rsponse\" instead of \"response\"\n}>()({\n  endpoint: \"/users/:userId\",\n  method: \"GET\",\n});\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n"
		},
		{
			"kind": "code",
			"text": "```ts\n// ✅ Correct usage — no lint error\nconst getUser = client.createRequest<{\n  response: User;\n}>()({\n  endpoint: \"/users/:userId\",\n  method: \"GET\",\n});\n```"
		},
		{
			"kind": "text",
			"text": "\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](https://github.com/BetterTyped/hyper-fetch/blob/main/License.md)"
		}
	],
